From: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:23:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] docs: Describe the CAN protocol trust model

The CAN protocol documentation explained reliability framing and UUID-based addressing without stating the security boundary.  That can invite readers to mistake the CAN CRC, Klipper message CRC, or hashed UUID for authentication mechanisms.

Document that CAN traffic is neither authenticated nor confidential and that its CRC and UUID fields are not credentials.  Enumerate the practical consequences of a device or host process gaining transmit access, including command injection, administration and bootloader requests, conflict shutdowns, observation, and denial of service.

Also identify the controls that must provide the actual boundary: physical protection, host permissions, and isolation from untrusted devices and networks.  Cryptographic protection would require a new protocol and key-provisioning design rather than reinterpretation of existing fields.

Signed-off-by: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>

